  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>X</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> denote the number of elements in set <math><mi>X</mi><mo>.</mo></math> Let <math><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> be a sample space, where each element is equally likely to occur. If <math><mi>A</mi></math> and <math><mi>B</mi></math> are independent events associated with <math><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo></math> then the number of ordered pairs <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> such that <math><mn>1</mn><mo>&#8804;</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#60;</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo></math> equals",
    "image": null
  },
